WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.560
It's very attractive to try to imply that
you're so familiar with this language

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.920
that you can use slang, but actually
you're getting ahead of yourself.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.380
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here today.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.330
And today I want to talk about
slang and swear words and why you

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.760
shouldn't deliberately learn them.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.110
Now, if you enjoy these videos,
please subscribe, click on

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.730
the bell for notifications.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:29.040
If you follow me on Spotify or some
other podcast service, please leave

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.630
a review, we much appreciate it.

00:00:31.049 --> 00:00:35.430
So many people when they learn a new
language, they're very motivated to

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.650
learn slang for some reason, or even
worse in my view, to learn swear words.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:47.550
And I don't recommend this personally,
when I learn a new language, I don't make

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:53.760
any effort to learn slang expressions and
certainly no effort to learn swear words.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.325
Uh, and there, there are
many reasons for this.

00:00:56.385 --> 00:01:02.655
First of all, I firmly believe that when
we learn a language, we want to learn

00:01:02.685 --> 00:01:05.865
the most neutral form of language we can.

00:01:06.345 --> 00:01:11.385
So we want to avoid
overly polite expressions.

00:01:11.595 --> 00:01:19.455
We want to avoid overly casual or rough
expressions or overly culturally specific,

00:01:19.665 --> 00:01:21.855
you know, sayings or expressions.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.880
And the reason is because it's very
difficult to use these things correctly.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:35.710
It is only when we are very comfortable
in the language when we fully understand

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:40.150
the impact of these expressions, the
nuance of how they should be used.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.970
It's only then that we can use
slang or swear words effectively.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:51.570
Uh, in fact, very often swear words,
you know, if you, if you use a very

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:56.960
gross swear word in a foreign language,
it doesn't strike you as that gross.

00:01:57.149 --> 00:02:00.660
For you it's as a learner, it's
kind of like a game, it's fun.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:04.859
Oh, look at me I can use
some gross swear word.

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:09.690
Uh, and yet the effect on the native
speaker is something that you can't

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:15.080
anticipate until you have enough cultural,
you know, experience with the language.

00:02:16.215 --> 00:02:19.035
And, uh, so, you know, in a way...

00:02:19.065 --> 00:02:24.704
and slang is the same way, uh, it's
very attractive to try to imply that

00:02:24.704 --> 00:02:28.424
you're so familiar with this language
that you can use slang, but actually

00:02:28.424 --> 00:02:33.015
you're getting ahead of yourself because
to use slang you actually have to be

00:02:33.015 --> 00:02:35.165
at quite a high level in the language.

00:02:35.165 --> 00:02:38.555
There is no shortcut to being able
to use these things and to that...

00:02:38.995 --> 00:02:44.355
to the, to some extent that's true of
all specialized form of a language.

00:02:44.355 --> 00:02:51.645
I see courses on business English or
other forms of English or in, in Canada,

00:02:51.645 --> 00:02:55.665
they try to teach immigrants, you know,
just that little bit of the language

00:02:55.665 --> 00:02:57.465
that they need for a specific job.

00:02:57.795 --> 00:03:01.710
And they have this whole system built
around the so called Canadian bench

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.410
marks, which I'm not a great fan of.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:09.960
And actually it's been my experience
that you have to elevate your whole game.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:13.605
You have to gradually improve in
the language, getting familiar

00:03:13.605 --> 00:03:17.085
with the language, improving your
oral comprehension, increasing

00:03:17.085 --> 00:03:20.655
your vocabulary, getting a better
and better sense of the language.

00:03:20.775 --> 00:03:24.195
And if you have that, if you have
that base and that language to

00:03:24.195 --> 00:03:29.295
add, uh, you know, business English
terms or scientific English terms

00:03:29.595 --> 00:03:32.445
or slang words is not so difficult.

00:03:32.535 --> 00:03:38.084
Once you have that firm base but if you
try to sort of short circuit the learning

00:03:38.114 --> 00:03:44.415
process, by wanting to show off your
knowledge of slang, there's a tremendous

00:03:44.415 --> 00:03:48.315
opportunity to fall flat on your face
and to make a negative impression.

00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:51.465
You know, at the other end of the
spectrum, say in Japanese where there

00:03:51.465 --> 00:03:56.234
is a lot of formal language, it's also
very difficult to sort of learn this

00:03:56.234 --> 00:03:59.295
formal language, you know, on its own.

00:03:59.295 --> 00:04:03.015
Like now I'm gonna to learn formal
words because you have to have a

00:04:03.015 --> 00:04:05.385
sense of when to use these words.

00:04:05.625 --> 00:04:09.225
And it's only when you've had enough
experience with the language, you've

00:04:09.225 --> 00:04:12.435
heard enough of the language, you've
been with people in different situations

00:04:13.394 --> 00:04:18.584
that you know how to use these
terms, whether it be polite language,

00:04:18.795 --> 00:04:21.284
slang, swear words, and so forth.

00:04:21.644 --> 00:04:25.965
And once you are able to use these
effectively, you will probably

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:29.175
have heard them so often that
you'll be comfortable using them.

00:04:29.175 --> 00:04:30.645
You'll be confident using them.

00:04:30.855 --> 00:04:35.474
So there's absolutely no purpose
in trying to deliberately learn

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:40.245
these terms as attractive as it, for
whatever reason, seems to some people,

00:04:40.545 --> 00:04:45.810
because there's so much opportunity
to create a bad impression by using,

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.310
especially swear words, but even
slang when it isn't appropriate.

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:56.610
So my advice is don't learn
slang, don't learn swear words.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:01.080
Once you have enough experience in the
language, once your overall level in

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:06.090
the language is high enough, you'll know
these terms, you will have heard them and

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:08.219
you'll be able to use them appropriately.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:14.625
So a little short message there, uh,
suggesting that people avoid embarrassment

00:05:14.625 --> 00:05:19.455
and don't go out deliberately
to learn slang or swear words.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:20.424
Thank you for listening.

